{"timestamp":"2026-09-01T05:28:44.347Z","ordinal":10213,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a05669-fc4c-7aa0-b9a1-034d833ed8ed","turn_id":"01a05b70-dc26-7a12-b7d4-0bd00dc336ef","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-edb59f00-6c24-4809-8df4-680cacae19b9","process_id":"85760","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","docker exec tiered-serve bash -c 'cd /root/projects/tiered-serve && sed -n \"1,360p\" tiered_serve/compression/core/p4flat.py | sed -n \"1,360p\" && grep -R -n \"host_encode.*p4\\|host_encode_blocks\\|P4FlatCPU\" tiered_serve cpp_extensions tests benchmarks --include=\"*.py\" --include=\"*.cpp\" --include=\"*.cu\" | head -160'"],"cwd":"file:///home/ubuntu","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"docker exec tiered-serve bash -c 'cd /root/projects/tiered-serve && sed -n \"1,360p\" tiered_serve/compression/core/p4flat.py | sed -n \"1,360p\" && grep -R -n \"host_encode.*p4\\|host_encode_blocks\\|P4FlatCPU\" tiered_serve cpp_extensions tests benchmarks --include=\"*.py\" --include=\"*.cpp\" --include=\"*.cu\" | head -160'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\"\"\"BF16 P4-flat weight compressor.\n\nPer-tile 16-entry exponent palette + 4-bit code + raw sign|mantissa byte.\nOut-of-palette exponents are stored as a separate (index, value) list and\nre-injected by a patch kernel during decompress — so the result is\nbit-exact-equivalent to the original BF16 weight.\n\nCompress runs on the GPU (one CTA per 64×64 tile).  Both compress and\ndecompress are delivered by the native PyTorch C++ extension\n``tiered_serve.cpp_exts.zipserv_p4flat_ext``.  No native fused\ndecompress+MM kernel: ``linear_apply`` falls through to the base class\ndefault (``decompress + F.linear``) which empirically beats every fused\nvariant on real LLM weights for decode-N shapes.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport logging\nimport os\nfrom typing import Dict, Optional\n\nimport torch\n\nfrom tiered_serve.compressor_base import TensorCompressor\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"vllm\")\n\n\ntry:\n    from tiered_serve.cpp_exts import zipserv_p4flat_ext as _p4f_ext\n    _HAS_P4FLAT = True\nexcept Exception as _e:\n    logger.warning(\n        f\"P4FlatCompressor disabled: failed to load \"\n        f\"zipserv_p4flat_ext ({type(_e).__name__}: {_e})\")\n    _p4f_ext = None\n    _HAS_P4FLAT = False\n\n\nclass CompressedP4FlatTensor:\n    \"\"\"Container around the native :class:`CompressedP4Flat` struct.\n\n    Mirrors GPU/host tensor fields onto Python instance attrs so the loader\n    can iterate ``_BUFFER_ATTRS`` and stage them through a pool, matching\n    the pattern used by :class:`CompressedZipServFP8GpuTensor`.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    _BUFFER_ATTRS = (\n        \"headers\", \"codes\", \"sign_mantissa\",\n        \"subtile_codec\",\n        \"exc_indices\", \"exc_values\",\n        \"exc_sorted_indices\", \"exc_sorted_values\",\n        \"exc_group_m\", \"exc_group_offsets\",\n    )\n    # Pre-computed (attr, d_attr) pairs — avoids 10 f-string allocations\n    # per .to() / register_temp_d_tensor call (320 calls/step → 3200 fewer\n    # transient str objects per decode step).\n    _BUFFER_ATTR_D_PAIRS = tuple((a, f\"_d_{a}\") for a in _BUFFER_ATTRS)\n\n    def __init__(self, c_struct):\n        self._c = c_struct\n        self.output_tensor: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None\n        # Cached narrow views into GPU staging buffers, created once in\n        # register_temp_d_tensor and reused by every .to() call.  Eliminates\n        # 10 view + 10 setattr(self._c, ...) per .to() call (320 calls/step\n        # → 6400 fewer transient Python objects per decode step).\n        self._h2d_views: Optional[tuple] = None\n        self._h2d_srcs: Optional[tuple] = None\n        self._gpu_buf_cache: Optional[tuple] = None\n        for attr in self._BUFFER_ATTRS:\n            setattr(self, attr, getattr(c_struct, attr))\n        for _attr, d_attr in self._BUFFER_ATTR_D_PAIRS:\n            setattr(self, d_attr, None)\n\n    @property\n    def M(self) -> int:\n        return int(self._c.M)\n\n    @property\n    def K(self) -> int:\n        return int(self._c.K)\n\n    @property\n    def num_exceptions(self) -> int:\n        return int(self._c.num_exceptions)\n\n    @property\n    def num_groups(self) -> int:\n        return int(self._c.num_groups)\n\n    @property\n    def nbytes(self) -> int:\n        return int(self._c.nbytes)\n\n    @property\n    def total_compressed_size(self) -> int:\n        return self.nbytes\n\n    @property\n    def original_size(self) -> int:\n        return self.M * self.K * 2  # BF16 = 2 bytes / element\n\n    def register_temp_d_tensor(self, temp_d: torch.Tensor,\n                               gpu_pool: Optional[Dict[str, torch.Tensor]] = None\n                               ) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Bind decompress destination + per-attr GPU staging slots.\n\n        Pre-creates narrow views into the GPU staging buffers and pushes\n        them into the C struct once, so the per-decode ``.to()`` only does\n        ``copy_`` — no f-strings, no view creation, no per-call setattr.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.output_tensor = temp_d\n        device = temp_d.device\n        views = []\n        for attr, d_attr in self._BUFFER_ATTR_D_PAIRS:\n            src = getattr(self, attr)\n            if gpu_pool is not None and attr in gpu_pool:\n                dst = gpu_pool[attr]\n            else:\n                dst = torch.empty_like(src, device=device)\n            setattr(self, d_attr, dst)\n            n = src.numel()\n            view = dst[:n] if n > 0 else dst\n            views.append(view)\n            # Set C struct tensor pointer once — the view object is reused\n            # across decode steps, so the pointer never changes.\n            setattr(self._c, attr, view)\n        self._h2d_views = tuple(views)\n        self._h2d_srcs = tuple(getattr(self, a) for a in self._BUFFER_ATTRS)\n        self._gpu_buf_cache = None  # invalidate get_gpu_buffers cache\n\n    def to_host(self, huge_page_allocator=None\n                ) -> \"CompressedP4FlatTensor\":\n        \"\"\"Move all compressed buffers to pinned/hugepage CPU memory.\"\"\"\n        for attr in self._BUFFER_ATTRS:\n            gpu_tensor = getattr(self, attr)\n            if gpu_tensor.numel() == 0:\n                cpu_tensor = gpu_tensor.to(\"cpu\")\n            elif huge_page_allocator is not None:\n                gpu_tensor = gpu_tensor.contiguous()\n                try:\n                    hp_tensor = huge_page_allocator.allocate(\n                        gpu_tensor.shape, gpu_tensor.stride(),\n                        gpu_tensor.dtype, page_type=\"weight\")\n                    hp_tensor.copy_(gpu_tensor)\n                    cpu_tensor = hp_tensor\n                except (MemoryError, ValueError):\n                    logger.warning(\n                        \"Hugepage exhausted for P4Flat to_host (attr=%s); \"\n                        \"falling back to pinned memory\", attr)\n                    cpu_tensor = gpu_tensor.to(\"cpu\").pin_memory()\n            else:\n                cpu_tensor = gpu_tensor.to(\"cpu\").pin_memory()\n            setattr(self, attr, cpu_tensor)\n            setattr(self._c, attr, cpu_tensor)\n        for _attr, d_attr in self._BUFFER_ATTR_D_PAIRS:\n            setattr(self, d_attr, None)\n        self._h2d_views = None\n        self._h2d_srcs = None\n        self._gpu_buf_cache = None\n        import gc\n        gc.collect()\n        torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n        return self\n\n    def to(self, device=\"cuda\", non_blocking=True) -> None:\n        \"\"\"H2D copy CPU-resident buffers into pre-bound GPU staging slots.\n\n        Hot path: called ~320×/step (4 components × ~80 layers).  Uses\n        pre-cached narrow views and source tensors from\n        ``register_temp_d_tensor`` and dispatches ALL 10 copies in a single\n        C++ call (``batch_h2d``), eliminating 10 Python → C++ frame\n        transitions per call (~2880/step) that were the dominant source of\n        CPython frame data-stack 16 KiB boundary crossings (mmap/munmap).\n        \"\"\"\n        del device\n        views = self._h2d_views\n        if views is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"CompressedP4FlatTensor.to(): call register_temp_d_tensor first\")\n        srcs = self._h2d_srcs\n        if srcs is None:\n            srcs = tuple(getattr(self, a) for a in self._BUFFER_ATTRS)\n            self._h2d_srcs = srcs\n        # Single C++ dispatch: copies all 10 (src, dst) pairs on the current\n        # CUDA stream without leaving this Python frame.\n        _p4f_ext.batch_h2d(srcs, views)\n\n    def get_gpu_buffers(self):\n        cache = self._gpu_buf_cache\n        if cache is not None:\n            return cache\n        views = self._h2d_views\n        if views is not None:\n            # Reuse the same narrow views created by register_temp_d_tensor\n            # — the data is updated in-place by .to(), so the views always\n            # reflect the latest GPU staging contents.\n            self._gpu_buf_cache = views\n            return views\n        out = []\n        for attr, d_attr in self._BUFFER_ATTR_D_PAIRS:\n            n = getattr(self, attr).numel()\n            dst = getattr(self, d_attr)\n            out.append(dst[:n] if n > 0 else dst)\n        cache = tuple(out)\n        self._gpu_buf_cache = cache\n        return cache\n\n\nclass P4FlatCompressor(TensorCompressor):\n    \"\"\"BF16 P4-flat weight compressor backed by tiered-serve's\n    ``zipserv_p4flat_ext`` PyTorch C++ extension.\n\n    Per-tile 16-entry exponent palette + 4-bit code + raw sign|mantissa\n    byte. Out-of-palette exponents are stored as a separate (index,\n    value) list and reinjected by the patch kernel during decompress\n    — so the result is bit-exact-equivalent to the original BF16\n    weight.\n\n    Compress runs on the GPU (one CTA per 64x64 tile).  M and K must be\n    multiples of 64.\n\n    With ``HAS_FUSED_MM = True`` the inference hot path (``--fused-mm`` +\n    frozen_compressed) routes the forward through :meth:`linear_apply`, which\n    fuses decode into the P4-RS register-A WGMMA GEMM (the same RS-mode recipe\n    as ublb-flat, applied to the p4flat codec).  For token counts above the\n    per-shape :meth:`_fused_max_n_for` threshold it falls back to decompress +\n    ``F.linear`` (faster in the prefill / compute-bound regime).  The fused path\n    is bit-exact: the rare out-of-palette exceptions (decoded with a wrong\n    exponent on the RS kernel) are restored by a sparse rank-1 correction\n    (``p4_exc_correct``).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    HAS_FUSED_MM = True\n    _warned_exc = False\n\n    def __init__(self, comp_stream: Optional[torch.cuda.Stream] = None):\n        super().__init__(comp_stream)\n        if not _HAS_P4FLAT:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"P4FlatCompressor requires tiered-serve's \"\n                \"zipserv_p4flat_ext extension to build successfully.\")\n        # Per-shape fused threshold lives in _fused_max_n_for / _FUSED_MAX_N_TABLE.\n        # tests/benchmarks may set this instance attr directly to force-fuse at\n        # all N.  ``decompress`` runs on the current stream (no comp_stream\n        # switch), CUDA-graph capture-safe, so a captured decode batch above a\n        # shape's threshold can fall back to decompress without breaking capture.\n        self._fused_max_n_override = None\n\n    def compress(\n        self,\n        weight: torch.Tensor,\n        decomp_output_tensor: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None,\n        comp_output_tensor: Optional[CompressedP4FlatTensor] = None,\n        _sync: bool = True,\n    ) -> CompressedP4FlatTensor:\n        del comp_output_tensor\n        if weight.dtype != torch.bfloat16:\n            raise TypeError(\n                f\"P4FlatCompressor expects bfloat16, got {weight.dtype}\")\n        if weight.ndim != 2:\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"P4FlatCompressor expects a 2-D tensor, got {tuple(weight.shape)}\")\n\n        c_struct = _p4f_ext.compress(weight)\n        comp = CompressedP4FlatTensor(c_struct)\n        if decomp_output_tensor is not None:\n            comp.output_tensor = decomp_output_tensor\n        if _sync:\n            ratio = weight.nbytes / max(1, comp.nbytes)\n            logger.info(\n                f\"P4Flat compress [{comp.M}x{comp.K}]: ratio={ratio:.2f}x  \"\n                f\"nbytes={comp.nbytes}  num_exceptions={comp.num_exceptions}\")\n        return comp\n\n    def decompress(\n        self,\n        comp: CompressedP4FlatTensor,\n        output: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None,\n        *,\n        begin_event: Optional[torch.cuda.Event] = None,\n        end_event: Optional[torch.cuda.Event] = None,\n    ) -> torch.Tensor:\n        if not isinstance(comp, CompressedP4FlatTensor):\n            raise TypeError(\n                f\"P4FlatCompressor.decompress expects CompressedP4FlatTensor, \"\n                f\"got {type(comp).__name__}\")\n        if output is None:\n            output = comp.output_tensor\n        # Single (current) stream — no comp_stream switch.  The decompressed\n        # weight is consumed immediately by the caller (F.linear), so running\n        # the decompress on a separate stream buys no overlap; it only (a) broke\n        # CUDA-graph capture (\"operation not permitted when stream is\n        # capturing\", since comp_stream isn't part of the capture) and (b) left\n        # a cross-stream ordering gap vs the consuming GEMM.  Running on the\n        # current stream is capture-safe and keeps decompress -> GEMM correctly\n        # ordered.  Timing events, when provided, record on the current stream.\n        if begin_event is not None:\n            begin_event.record()\n        result = _p4f_ext.decompress(comp._c, output)\n        if end_event is not None:\n            end_event.record()\n        return result\n\n    def compress_batch(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        return super().compress_batch(*args, **kwargs)\n\n    def decompress_batch(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        return super().decompress_batch(*args, **kwargs)\n\n    # Per-(M, K) fused threshold: use the P4-RS fused kernel for N <= value,\n    # else decompress + cuBLAS.  These MUST be tuned in the engine, not in an\n    # isolated GEMM bench: decomp+cuBLAS writes the full reconstructed BF16\n    # weight to HBM (O 134MB, Down 470MB, GateUp 940MB), and in the serving\n    # engine that write contends with the concurrent weight-offload H2D on the\n    # HBM write path.  An isolated sweep (/tmp/thr_sweep.py) has no H2D overlap\n    # so it wrongly favours decomp for O/Down; in-engine batch-128 the fused\n    # path (no HBM write, no contention) is faster for O/GateUp/Down.  Measured\n    # in-engine (vllm_offload_kvweight --batch 128):\n    # In-engine TPOT (vllm_offload_kvweight --batch N), measured 2026-06-05:\n    #   batch 128: O/GU/Down fused, QKV decomp = 189.65ms (all-fused incl QKV\n    #     192.30 -> QKV's RS kernel is too slow even with contention; decomp\n    #     O/Down per isolated-optimal = 194.20 -> WORSE, contention dominates).\n    #   batch 256: GU/Down fused (256) = 321.67 vs GU/Down decomp (192) = 331.11\n    #     -> fusing wins by 9.4ms even at N=256 (isolated bench says decomp here,\n    #     but the engine HBM-write contention flips it).\n    # That measurement supported fusing O/GateUp/Down broadly, but keep the\n    # live table scoped to the batch-128 serving range we are validating now;\n    # N>256 (prefill) decompresses anyway via fallback.\n    # The isolated+H2D benchmark below crossed over to decompress+cuBLAS earlier\n    # for O/Down, but the batch-128 serving trace regressed in exactly that\n    # region: dense materialization pushes the frozen-weight scheduling gap into\n    # every decode graph.  Keep QKV conservative, but restore O/Down to the\n    # in-engine batch-128 fused rang